## 🔐 Area 1: Authentication Failure (AUTH)

### TC-NEG-AUTH-01 | Direct URL Access Without Login

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-AUTH-01 |
| **AC Reference** | AC1 — Member must be authenticated. Guest access not permitted |
| **Scenario** | Unauthenticated user attempts to access Pharmacy Benefit Checker via direct URL |
| **Pre-conditions** | User is NOT logged in. Feature URL is known |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Open browser in incognito/private mode. 2. Copy and paste the Pharmacy Benefit Checker URL directly into the address bar. 3. Press Enter. 4. Observe system behavior |
| **Expected Result** | System immediately redirects to the member login page. No drug data, formulary results, or UI elements of the feature are exposed |
| **Pass Criteria** | Redirect to login occurs. Zero benefit data visible to unauthenticated user |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

---

### TC-NEG-AUTH-02 | Expired Session Mid-Search

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-AUTH-02 |
| **AC Reference** | AC1 — Authentication required throughout the session |
| **Scenario** | Member's session token expires while actively using the Pharmacy Benefit Checker |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member is logged in. Session timeout is configurable in test environment |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Log in as a valid member. 2. Navigate to Pharmacy Benefit Checker. 3. Let the session expire (or manually invalidate the auth token via dev tools). 4. Enter a valid drug name. 5. Click Search. 6. Observe system response |
| **Expected Result** | System detects the expired session before returning results. Member is redirected to login with a session expiry message. No formulary data is returned |
| **Pass Criteria** | No data returned on expired session. Login redirect occurs. Session expiry message displayed |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

