## 🏥 Area 3: Plan Type Edge Cases (PLAN)

### TC-NEG-PLAN-01 | Stale Data Served Without Timestamp — Batch Cache Plan

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-PLAN-01 |
| **AC Reference** | AC5 — Batch-cache plan members must see last-updated timestamp |
| **Scenario** | Member on HMO Classic plan receives formulary results but no last-updated timestamp is displayed |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member logged in on HMO Classic plan. Nightly batch has run. Timestamp rendering is being tested |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Log in as an HMO Classic member. 2. Navigate to Pharmacy Benefit Checker. 3. Search for a known drug. 4. Inspect the results screen for the presence of a last-updated timestamp. 5. Repeat for PPO Select and CHIP plan members |
| **Expected Result** | Every result for HMO Classic, PPO Select, and CHIP members includes a visible last-updated timestamp. Absence of timestamp = defect |
| **Pass Criteria** | Timestamp present for all 3 batch-cache plan types. Missing timestamp on any batch-cache result = FAIL |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

---

### TC-NEG-PLAN-02 | Batch Cache Failure — No Data Refresh Overnight

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-PLAN-02 |
| **AC Reference** | AC5, AC6 — Data freshness and real-time vs batch distinction |
| **Scenario** | Nightly batch job fails — HMO Classic member searches and receives either no results or silently stale data with no warning |
| **Pre-conditions** | Batch cache job simulated as failed in test environment. Member on HMO Classic plan is logged in |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Simulate batch cache failure (disable or skip nightly refresh in test env). 2. Log in as HMO Classic member. 3. Search for a drug. 4. Observe: (a) whether results are displayed, (b) whether a staleness warning is shown, (c) whether the timestamp reflects the last successful batch |
| **Expected Result** | System either: (a) shows last known data WITH a clear staleness warning and the timestamp of the last successful run, OR (b) displays a message that data is temporarily unavailable. It must NOT silently serve outdated data |
| **Pass Criteria** | Silent stale data with no warning = FAIL. Member must always know data currency status |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

---

### TC-NEG-PLAN-03 | Batch Cache Timestamp Shown for Real-Time Plan Member

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-PLAN-03 |
| **AC Reference** | AC5, AC6 — Timestamp only for batch-cache plans |
| **Scenario** | Member on a real-time plan incorrectly sees a batch-cache last-updated timestamp — indicating plan type misdetection |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member is logged in on a standard real-time plan (not HMO Classic, PPO Select, or CHIP) |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Log in as a member on a real-time plan. 2. Navigate to Pharmacy Benefit Checker. 3. Search for a known drug. 4. Inspect results screen for presence of a last-updated timestamp |
| **Expected Result** | No last-updated timestamp appears for real-time plan members. Results display without any batch-cache staleness indicator |
| **Pass Criteria** | Timestamp field absent for real-time plan members. Presence of timestamp = plan type detection bug |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

