## 🔌 Area 5: API Failure Scenarios (API)

### TC-NEG-API-01 | Formulary API Completely Unavailable

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-API-01 |
| **AC Reference** | AC3, AC6 — Results depend on formulary API availability |
| **Scenario** | Formulary API is down — member searches for a drug and receives no response from the API |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member is logged in. Formulary API is simulated as unavailable (timeout or connection refused) in test environment |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Simulate formulary API downtime in test environment. 2. Log in as a valid member. 3. Navigate to Pharmacy Benefit Checker. 4. Search for a known drug. 5. Observe system behavior — does it wait, timeout, or show an error? |
| **Expected Result** | System displays a user-friendly error message indicating the service is temporarily unavailable. No raw API error, stack trace, or technical message is exposed to the member |
| **Pass Criteria** | Member-facing error message shown. No raw error exposed. No indefinite loading spinner with no feedback |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

