### TC-NEG-API-03 | Formulary API Returns Malformed Response

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-API-03 |
| **AC Reference** | AC3 — All result fields must be present and correctly rendered |
| **Scenario** | Formulary API returns a 200 OK response but the payload is malformed — missing required fields or unexpected data types |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member is logged in. Test environment configured to return a malformed API response (e.g., tier field returns a string instead of integer, or JSON is incomplete) |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Configure test environment to return malformed API payload. 2. Log in as a valid member. 3. Search for a drug. 4. Observe whether the system: (a) crashes, (b) renders partial data, (c) handles gracefully with an error message |
| **Expected Result** | System detects the malformed response and displays a generic error message to the member. No partial or corrupted data is displayed. No raw JSON or technical error is shown |
| **Pass Criteria** | No partial data rendered. No raw error exposed. Member-friendly fallback message shown |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

