### TC-NEG-API-04 | Batch Cache Not Populated — Morning Access Before First Run

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Test ID** | TC-NEG-API-04 |
| **AC Reference** | AC5 — Batch cache data must include last-updated timestamp |
| **Scenario** | Member on HMO Classic accesses the feature before the nightly batch job has completed for the first time (e.g., new environment setup or first day after go-live) |
| **Pre-conditions** | Member on HMO Classic plan. Batch cache has never been populated in the environment |
| **Test Steps** | 1. Set up a clean test environment with no batch cache data. 2. Log in as an HMO Classic member. 3. Navigate to Pharmacy Benefit Checker. 4. Search for a drug. 5. Observe system response — does it error, show empty results, or display a meaningful message? |
| **Expected Result** | System recognizes empty cache state and displays a meaningful message (e.g., "Formulary data is not yet available. Please check back later."). It must NOT show empty results silently or crash |
| **Pass Criteria** | Meaningful message shown. No silent empty result. No system error exposed to member |
| **Severity** | 🔴 High |

